# The pinned source of the Psiphon client that a release of Postern builds
# (Ruling S2-26; docs/third-party/psiphon-tunnel-core.md). scripts/psiphon-core.sh
# reads it, and so does a test of internal/panel/releases, which checks it
# against builtin.json and package psiphoncore. Change all of them together:
# a new commit is a new version of psiphon-core, with new SHA-256s.
#
# PSIPHON_CORE_COMMIT      the commit of github.com/Psiphon-Labs/psiphon-tunnel-core
# PSIPHON_CORE_SOURCE_SHA256  the SHA-256 of the source archive of that commit
#                          (https://codeload.github.com/.../tar.gz/<commit>)
# PSIPHON_CORE_GO          the Go toolchain of its go.mod (toolchain), which its
#                          psiphon-tls needs exactly
# PSIPHON_CORE_DATE        the date of the commit, the build date of the binary
# PSIPHON_CORE_VERSION     the version of psiphon-core in the catalog
PSIPHON_CORE_COMMIT=c4a09096ab401b57f52e092c8f2f829c8fac7628
PSIPHON_CORE_SOURCE_SHA256=35522b4b5e8b39acfaad6fcc5a98b5164cea9eb8ae5a6e5c691270b87f42dd0f
PSIPHON_CORE_GO=go1.26.8
PSIPHON_CORE_DATE=2026-10-05T17:02:09Z
PSIPHON_CORE_VERSION=20261005-c4a09096ab
